✅ Addressed in commits 02b1617 to f0a8aeb

**WARNING:** No containment check after normalization - `..` in `RelativePath` escapes the user data tree

`Path.GetFullPath` resolves `..`/`.` segments, but the result is never validated to stay under `userDataBasePath`. A manifest entry such as `..\..\startup.ini` yields a `targetPath` outside the user data directory, and `InstallUserDataAsync` then backs up, deletes, and materializes files at that location. `RelativePath` originates from acquired and persisted content manifests (including entries re-registered by `ProfileContentLinkerService`), so a malicious or corrupt content package can overwrite files outside the tracked user data tree (zip-slip). Now that the path is eagerly normalized here, the check is cheap:

```csharp
var fullPath = Path.GetFullPath(targetPath);
var basePath = Path.TrimEndingDirectorySeparator(Path.GetFullPath(userDataBasePath));
if (!fullPath.StartsWith(basePath + Path.DirectorySeparatorChar, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
{
    throw new InvalidOperationException($"Relative path escapes the user data directory: {relativePath}");
}

return fullPath;
```

The throw is caught by the caller's outer catch and converted into a failed `OperationResult`, which is the correct outcome for an invalid manifest path.

---
Reply with `@kilocode-bot fix it` to have Kilo Code address this issue.

_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Make provider registration atomic.**

Line 293 checks for an existing provider and then adds the provider without `_providerLock`. `ConcurrentBag<T>` only protects individual operations. Two concurrent calls can both pass `All` and register the same `SourceName`.

Use the same lock as `UnregisterProvider`. Duplicate providers cause duplicate searches and make `FirstOrDefault` provider selection ambiguous.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 public void RegisterProvider(IContentProvider provider)
 {
     ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(provider);

-    if (_providers.All(p => p.SourceName != provider.SourceName))
+    lock (_providerLock)
     {
-        _providers.Add(provider);
-        _logger.LogInformation("Registered content provider: {ProviderName}", provider.SourceName);
-    }
-    else
-    {
-        _logger.LogWarning("Attempted to register duplicate provider: {ProviderName}", provider.SourceName);
+        if (_providers.All(p => p.SourceName != provider.SourceName))
+        {
+            _providers.Add(provider);
+            _logger.LogInformation("Registered content provider: {ProviderName}", provider.SourceName);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            _logger.LogWarning("Attempted to register duplicate provider: {ProviderName}", provider.SourceName);
+        }
     }
 }
```
